266
00:18:10,170 --> 00:18:12,840
...why didn't I get the honey-glazed ham?

267
00:18:13,090 --> 00:18:16,670
Or I didn't spend enough on flowers. If I spent more, she'd say:

268
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:20,300
"Why waste your money? I don't need flowers, I'm dead."

269
00:18:21,220 --> 00:18:22,930
That sounds like Nana.

270
00:18:24,430 --> 00:18:26,970
Do you know what it's like to grow up...

271
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:31,940
...with someone who is critical of every single thing you say?

272
00:18:34,570 --> 00:18:35,730
I can imagine.

273
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:39,820
I tell you, it's a wonder your mother turned out...

274
00:18:40,070 --> 00:18:43,200
...to be the positive, life-affirming person she is.

275
00:18:44,990 --> 00:18:46,990
That is a wonder.

276
00:18:49,580 --> 00:18:54,380
So tell me something, Mom. If you had to do it all over again...

277
00:18:54,630 --> 00:18:57,670
...I mean, if she was here right now...

278
00:18:58,220 --> 00:18:59,420
...would you tell her?

279
00:19:00,010 --> 00:19:01,050
Tell her what?

280
00:19:02,510 --> 00:19:07,010
How she drove you crazy, picking on every little detail.

281
00:19:07,430 --> 00:19:09,310
Like your hair, for example.

282
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:13,770
I'm not sure I know what you're getting at.

283
00:19:15,230 --> 00:19:18,820
Would things have been better if you'd just told her the truth?

284
00:19:22,570 --> 00:19:23,740
No.

285
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:28,080
I think some things are better left unsaid.

286
00:19:28,330 --> 00:19:31,210
I think it's nicer when people just get along.

287
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,130
Ha.

288
00:19:35,290 --> 00:19:36,420
More wine, dear?

289
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,500
Oh, I think so.

290
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:49,430
Those earrings look really lovely on you.

291
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:52,850
Thank you.

292
00:19:53,810 --> 00:19:54,940
They're yours.

293
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:57,940
Actually, they were Nana's.

294
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:01,150
No!

295
00:20:02,570 --> 00:20:04,360
Now I'm depressed.

296
00:20:08,830 --> 00:20:11,040
Even more than I was.

297
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:20,840
Hey, who's this little naked guy?

298
00:20:21,050 --> 00:20:23,170
Uh, that little naked guy would be me.

299
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:26,550
Aw. Look at the little thing.

300
00:20:29,390 --> 00:20:31,970
Yes, fine. That is my penis.

301
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:34,600
Can we be grownups now?

302
00:20:35,310 --> 00:20:37,810
- Who are those people?     - Got me.

303
00:20:38,110 --> 00:20:41,570
- That's Nana right there in the middle.     - Wow.

304
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:42,900
Yeah, let's see.

305
00:20:43,150 --> 00:20:45,820
"Me and the gang at Java Joe's."

306
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:48,200
Wow. Monica, you look just like your grandmother.

307
00:20:48,450 --> 00:20:49,620
How old was she there?

308
00:20:49,830 --> 00:20:51,740
Let's see. "1939."

309
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:54,000
Uh, twenty-four, twenty-five.

310
00:20:54,210 --> 00:20:57,080
Huh. It looks like a fun gang.

311
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:06,130
Ooh, look, look, look. I got Monica naked.

312
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:07,840
Let me see.

313
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:12,350
No, no. That would be me again.

314
00:21:17,230 --> 00:21:19,560
I'm, uh, just trying something.

315
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:32,740
- Hey, Lowell.     - Oh, hey, Chandler.

316
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:37,420
So how's it going in Financial Services?

317
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:40,960
It's like Mardi Gras without the papier-mâché heads.

318
00:21:41,210 --> 00:21:42,300
How about you?

319
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:46,170
Good. Good. Listen, um, heh...

320
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:49,470
...I don't know what Shelly told you about me, but, uh...

321
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:51,970
...I'm not.

322
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:55,310
I know. That's what I told her.

323
00:21:55,810 --> 00:21:56,980
- Really?     - Yeah.

324
00:21:58,310 --> 00:22:00,060
So you can tell?

325
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:06,320
Pretty much. Most of the time. We have a kind of radar.

326
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:10,030
So you don't think I have...

327
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:11,240
...a quality?

328
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:16,080
Speaking for my people, I'd have to say no.

329
00:22:18,620 --> 00:22:21,880
By the way, your friend Brian from Payroll? He is.

330
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:23,500
- He is?     - Yep.

331
00:22:23,710 --> 00:22:25,630
And way out of your league.

332
00:22:29,380 --> 00:22:30,970
Out of my league.

333
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:35,350
I could get a Brian. If I wanted to get a Brian, I could get a Brian.

334
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:37,430
Hey, Brian.

